## Verification after integration

Run the crate's twin_text_date and clock_exports_use_the_current_local_calendar,
then twin_live_text_date with MIXDOG_NODE_TREE=C:/Project/mixdog.
The recorder accepts --write to recreate only this task's owned fixture files;
without --write it emits JSON on stdout without mutating any file.

Known shared-core follow-up: Value::Text(String) cannot retain isolated UTF-16
surrogates produced by LEFT/RIGHT/MID/CHAR/UNICHAR. The golden retains raw UTF-16
units and replay intentionally reports those differences rather than accepting
replacement characters as equivalent. Shared Value/coerce changes are root-owned.
Original xmlEncode only escapes the five XML punctuation characters; it does not
normalise surrogates. Recombining LEFT("😀",1)&RIGHT("😀",1) happens before output
encoding and is observably different if each intermediate is made well-formed.
At the final ZIP boundary, portable-opc.mjs calls generateAsync(type:nodebuffer).
JSZip lib/utf8.js:169 uses nodejsUtils.newBufferFrom -> Buffer.from(str,"utf-8"),
which replaces unpaired surrogates. A lone CHAR surrogate directly emitted is
therefore the same final U+FFFD bytes; concatenation and CODE/UNICODE before that
boundary remain different. The original-engine fixture records xmlUtf8 as well
as the unsanitized UTF-16 units to keep these cases distinct.


## Corrective follow-up after independent review

Public regex paths now use mixdog_js::JsRegex (regex is a private module).
DSUM preserves nested-array subtotal order; DAVERAGE performs default ToPrimitive
before addition. SORT uses the existing V8 js_sort_by and exactly the source's
nonzero tie comparator and relational coercion. Large finite DATE components are
checked against V8 MakeDay bounds and computed in i128 before any shared i64 time
helper; huge invalid dates return Invalid Date instead of overflowing. REPT checks
V8's 64-bit maximum UTF-16 string length before allocation and uses fallible reserve.
The recorder measures buffer.constants.MAX_STRING_LENGTH and pins the expected value.
Large REPT reference cases are over that limit, and throw before output allocation;
they have a one-second VM execution bound that is not encoded as an accepted result.

The previous reviewer claim about YEARFRAC month numbering was incorrect. The
original source itself uses getMonth()+1 followed by em===1 && ed===29. That
January-29 quirk is preserved, not corrected to textbook February logic. Original
recordings pin 2023-03-01 -> 2024-02-29 basis 1 to 1, and the January-29 case as well.

The twin now compares all JSON/IEEE-754 bit fields exactly, including NaN sign and
payload. No equivalence rule hides arithmetic or representation differences.
Known UTF-16 mismatches remain acceptance blockers, as described above.

### Additional shared Date string prerequisite (root-owned; no shared edits here)

File: mixdog-xlsx-formula/src/coerce.rs, date_to_string / to_js_string(Value::Date)
Current helper omits the parenthesized time-zone name from Date.prototype.toString.
Required: return V8's complete local Date string (including the correct daylight/
standard zone display name for that instant, negative/extended year formatting,
and Invalid Date). Route through an authoritative shared JS Date string helper;
do not approximate by appending a fixed offset label. Existing local calendar
conversion APIs alone do not provide the V8 display name.

Exact reference examples are recorded as sharedDateStringCases in golden.json:
CONCAT(Date(0)) and REPT(Date(0),1) in UTC and America/New_York. Zone display
names are localized by the original process's default locale (this recorder host
uses Korean names). Do not hard-code the English Coordinated Universal Time or
Eastern Standard Time labels. The full original strings are in the golden;
referenceLocale records the locale for reproducibility.
These cases are not ignored or normalized, so full replay remains blocked until
the shared helper and UTF-16 representation work land. DAVERAGE's final numeric
NaN is unaffected by the spelling of that suffix; string-returning functions are.

Node fixture regeneration and rustfmt completed. No Rust compile/test/build or
commit was run. Lead should re-index this set's new manifest/hash and run strict
library + engine/XML replay after all shared prerequisites and registration land.
